    "answer": {
        "text": "§\nWhat type of seizures can be treated with broad spectrum antiepileptics?\n\n(1) Focal seizures\n(2) Generalized seizure\n\n(3) Juvenile myoclonic seizure\n\n(4) Abscence seizures (less so)\n\n[Image: 5bf8a49bb543662493b26188f7f35f9793898d47418d5e87265e7aa779e983d1]\n\n[Image: 7f41a6c8034ae3c9a366fc70d90faf1d8b386dc2d1edeedd6729af5ed52a28d7]\n\n[Image: f7bcc6c1ea3c72604b231843ee9607177ddee0173c4b376abb0abe620fa1632d]\n\n4.2 - Valproate, topiramate, lamotrigine, levetiracetam\n[Image: b6de6841506ab44b40652032e6f4399bd43ac8406f2030d1079500c79bf295cc]\n\n[Image: b8b1970180a64ab677591daccf17df025d56a38b8299d8e02740e57c40193d7c]\n\n[Image: c3043f3c2f396c1132e341dc2c19a439589ba89eef0f5980c4f478d378b35668]\n\n[Image: 2bab7a24324cb36e7d3115a5c4ada1905c53d6eb86e4080b17774ff251e1158a]\n\n[Image: fb3ad4700cf08245689b08fc53ae5cccaa6480e193f08f2f661cc14acd0021f5]",
